        <mxCell id="c4-note" value="One login table serves all six roles. patient and doctor each sign in through AT MOST ONE account — that is the 1:1 on those two lines, and the UNIQUE on user_account.patient_id and .doctor_id. Which of the three links applies is decided by the role, so it is checked by a trigger: a MySQL CHECK cannot read another table. web_session (7 Nov 2026): one account opens many sessions, each identified by a SHA-256 of its session id; switching an account off deletes its sessions." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=24;fontColor=#47606D;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#D3DEE3;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="220" y="1370" width="1500" height="260" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
